						 	 Key Responsibilities 




 
	     


         The Town Clerk serves the community in several key administrative capacities, acting as the Town’s: Chief Election Official:  Oversees all municipal, state, and federal election processes. Recording Officer:  Standardizes, logs, and protects the official history and official actions of the Town. Registrar of Vital Records and Statistics:  Manages and issues certificates for local births, marriages, and deaths. Public Records Access Officer (RAO):  Coordinates and processes all municipal public records requests. Licensing Officer:  Issues various town permits, certificates, and municipal business licenses. In addition to these statutory duties, the Town Clerk’s office serves as a  primary access point  connecting Belmont’s inhabitants to the Commonwealth of Massachusetts and the Federal Government.  The Town Clerk is  elected to renewable three-year terms  with a salary voted upon at each Annual Town Meeting. 
     

 
